body:
给 #3593 的四失败用例正式语义依据（不要求盲改 expected）：



The bounded semantic correction is commit `44cfc4e0b4f2abb5d503e5f2f6bd441526c58aca`, preserved on task/3654-canonical-projection and included in compiler source candidate `f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd` / https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/pull/3916 . It is separate from the format-only correction. Diff: two test files, three edited assertion sites,6 insertions/3 deletions; one count site covers two original theory cases. No production file or case roster changes.

Two current-document retry cases

Original test fixture returns `null` then the exact AOT entry for `aot-cold-wait` and `aot-shared-budget`: [fixture](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/blob/f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd/tests/backend/Unit/CanonicalArticleProjectionVerifierTests.cs#L452 ). The shared-budget fixture still checks the very same caller CancellationToken.

Production `ReadAotOutputAsync` calls TryGetEntryAsync at946 and immediately returns `aot_current_document_missing` if entry null at955–957. It cannot obtain a sidecar key/hash or read hydration bytes at this stage. Only after a real entry and valid unique DOM marker are available does it call publicArtifactStorage.TryReadAsync at1004–1006: [sole original production observer](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/blob/f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd/src/backend/Services/Fixtures/CanonicalArticleProjectionVerifier.cs#L927).

Therefore original two missing-then-present theory cases have exactly TWO document lookups and ONE hydration read. Change only sidecar expected count for those two scenarios; retain readCount2 for projection/artifact/cache/document, and retain every other scenario's sidecar count unchanged. Requiring2 hydration reads on the absent-document branch would require inventing a marker or scheduling an unnecessary duplicate current sidecar read, which contradicts current source. It is not a partial document acceptance or a weakened sidecar integrity check.

Original retry catches ONLY exact pair `aot_current_document_missing` and `projection_aggregate_contains_failures`, within same bounded caller token, and makes stale/invalid bytes or other failure terminal: [original retry gate](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/blob/f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd/src/backend/Services/Fixtures/CanonicalArticleProjectionVerifier.cs#L211).

Authority: [current issue3654](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/issues/3654), Acceptance2–3 require real original mapper/output coordinates and existing semantics preserved; [current issue2175](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/issues/2175), deliverables3/6/8/10 require actual current AOT/digests/fail-closed/timeouts/current refs/independent reread. Neither requires a hydration storage call before any AOT document/sidecar reference exists. [Existing sidecar contract](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/blob/f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd/docs/api/contracts.md#L1924) obtains sidecar from HTML marker; current read is by that exact content-hash reference.

All original negative roster retained: document missing, hydration missing, stale publication/revision/right coordinates, content/metadata/byte/digest drift, duplicate data IDs, comment/rawtext/template/foreign-script marker spoof, inline shadow/external URL, shared original token, never-completing read, caller cancellation and terminal aggregate failures. In particular missing sidecar continues `aot_hydration_payload_invalid`; missing doc continues `aot_current_document_missing`, never success.

Two startup detail cases

Production startup plan already awaits migrationRunner.RunAsync then returns `StartupTaskOutcome.Ok("current_schema_verified")`: [original production steps87–89](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/blob/f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd/src/backend/Infrastructure/Bootstrap/LifecycleHostedBootstrapService.cs#L81). Correct only expected detail strings at test116 and165 from compatibility_check to the actual original status; unchanged other cache/rollback/status and Received(1) assertions: [tests](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/blob/f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd/tests/backend/Unit/LifecycleHostedBootstrapServiceTests.cs#L100).

The actual production DI binds ISchemaMigrationRunner to CurrentSchemaStartupVerifier: [Program148](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/blob/f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd/src/backend/Program.cs#L148), [canonical registration171](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/blob/f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd/src/backend/Infrastructure/Bootstrap/RuntimeSecurityAndLifecycleServiceCollectionExtensions.cs#L171). Its RunAsync clears admission, verifies explicit receipt path/file SHA/candidate revision against live DB/model, checks cancellation then publishes verified admission; failures are fatal fixed-category errors: [runner73–91](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/blob/f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd/src/backend/Infrastructure/SchemaMigration/SchemaMigrationRunner.cs#L73). It is not an old generic compatibility-only step.

Formal contract: [current database migration contract523 onward](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/blob/f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd/docs/database-migration.md#L523) requires explicit absolute receipt path, complete SHA and exact source revision rather than latest aliases; [#3654 acceptance3](https://github.com/Ozwasyd/FsusBlog/issues/3654) explicitly preserves existing lifecycle/worker/receipt/protocol semantics. No new requirement has been written or old failure waived. Runner failure still stops later tasks, failure Detail remains InvalidOperationException in original failure fixture, original development vs production handling and rollback controls unchanged. A mocked runner success in this unit test does NOT prove real schema receipt or DB runtime qualification. Our actual original isolated PG lane at exactf53 exits1 at recipe syntax before publication-fault and remains blocked.

Byte identity and retained failures

`git diff 3bc9bacd55b4453ed0abd48632c6a1bb3f7944f8..f53b6b79f8cf051bd190cad2e49a57ea4a1cc1bd --` the three production owners is EMPTY. SHA256 each also identical at currentd1f8a4e95348039d9db4cbcefce57d406399dc21:
- CanonicalArticleProjectionVerifier.cs:3bf38274e9b805302b198fd8722b0232e3278ad74d6fbc2fae66cfb986c23b74
- LifecycleHostedBootstrapService.cs:1f8124fae0e5125e3c448722565d9b3a23af8ee5c86372c4ce1298a345078510
- SchemaMigrationRunner.cs:d4ffa1dbb1c183fdf9199b9fa8a9457bf51094429d728fc0557141e3387d5540

Original248 run before assertion correction remains raw244pass/4fail in compiler-candidate/results/bounded-compiler.trx; original351 run347pass/4fail is also retained. Corrected final exactf53 original248/248 and currentd1f8 original396/396 are existing evidence, no extra rerun requested for this review. No old receipt is promoted to schema/runtime/product acceptance. Consumers should review minimal semantic diff independently; don't blindly substitute expected values.

